    "event": "Flood Warning",
    "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
    "senderName": "NWS Albuquerque NM",
    "headline": "Flood Warning issued October 28 at 6:40PM MDT until October 29 at 6:45PM MDT by NWS Albuquerque NM",
    "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is occurring.\n\n* WHERE...South Central Socorro County in central New Mexico...\n\n* WHEN...Until 645 PM MDT Thursday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying\nand flood-prone locations is imminent or occurring.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 638 PM MDT, emergency management reported flooding in the\nwarned area. Flooding is already occurring.\n- Flooding was reported in Socorro County in the Escondida and\nPueblito Communities. Several roads have been rendered impassible\nnear San Pedro.\n- Some locations that will experience ",
    "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe especially cautious at night when it is harder to recognize the\ndangers of flooding.",
    "response": "Avoid",
    "note": null,
